ONE LOCAL CHANGE in stb_image_write.h. In
stbiw__jpg_writeBits, `bitBuf` is an int and `bitBuf <<= 8` overflows it, which
is undefined behaviour in C; the host tests' -fsanitize=undefined reports it.
Only bits 16..23 of bitBuf are ever read, so masking to 24 bits in unsigned
arithmetic gives the same bytes. Checked: a 640x480 test frame encodes to a
byte-identical JPEG with the upstream and patched headers (gcc, 2026-09-27).

-      bitBuf <<= 8;
+      bitBuf = (int)(((unsigned)bitBuf << 8) & 0xffffffu); /* tt7cam: was bitBuf <<= 8 (signed overflow, UB) */

